# lastgenie - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
I am creating an Ecommerce website for brand name Genie. Its a sexual enhancer drink designed for male and female. 
Product information:
Male sexual enhancer - 50ML bottle (1 sku) - 10$
Female sexual enhancer - 50ML bottle (1sku) - 10$
Users can also buy it in 12 pack of each - $99

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: Next.js with Tailwind CSS
- Backend: Express on Node.js
- Database: SQLite with Prisma ORM
- Deployment: aws amplify

## Coding Standards
- Use TypeScript for all files
- Follow ESLint and Prettier configurations
- Write comprehensive JSDoc comments for functions
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Prefer functional components with hooks

## File Structure
- `/client` - Frontend React application
- `/server` - Backend API and services
- `/shared` - Shared types and schemas

## Component Patterns
- Use shadcn/ui components from `@/components/ui`
- Follow atomic design principles
- Keep components small and focused

## API Conventions
- RESTful endpoints under `/api`
- Use Zod for request validation
- Return consistent JSON response formats

## Database Guidelines
- Use Prisma ORM for all database operations
- Define schemas in `server/prisma/schema.prisma`
- Use Prisma migrations for schema changes (`npm run db:migrate`)
- Development database: SQLite (`server/dev.db`)
- Seed database with `npm run db:seed`
- Never use `db:push` in production - always use migrations


## Authentication
- Methods: email with JWT tokens
- Secure all protected routes with middleware
- JWT tokens stored in HTTP-only cookies
- Role-based authorization (customer, admin, super_admin)



## Realtime Features
- Technology: null
- Handle connection state gracefully


## Testing
- Write unit tests for utility functions
- Use integration tests for API endpoints
- Test components with React Testing Library
